# Dark Depths has its ice counters removed by Vampire Hexmage and its state trigger goes on the stack; Bot2 destroys it with
# Strip Mine in response. When the trigger resolves Dark Depths is a new object in the graveyard (CR 400.7), so it can't be
# sacrificed, and "If you do" makes no Marit Lage (CR 608.2c; the ruling: "If Dark Depths leaves the battlefield before its
# triggered ability resolves, you won't be able to sacrifice it, so you won't create Marit Lage").

[Bot1 Deck]
Dark Depths
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Vampire Hexmage
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Strip Mine
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Dark Depths.Play
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Vampire Hexmage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Vampire Hexmage.Activate(Dark Depths)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack = Dark Depths
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Dark Depths; Ability: Destroy)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet
Bot1.Graveyard = Dark Depths; Vampire Hexmage; Black Lotus
Stack.Count = 0
